## 🏃 How to run

This repo ships three GGUF files, so always pass `--hf-file` to pick one explicitly. Example usage
with llama.cpp (QAT `Q4_1`, the recommended on-device quant):

```
llama-cli -hf taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-GGUF \
    --hf-file MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Instruct-Q4_1.gguf \
    --temp 0.8 --top-p 0.8 --top-k 20
```

Local server (OpenAI-compatible endpoint):

```
llama-server -hf taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-GGUF --hf-file MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Instruct-Q4_1.gguf \
    -c 4096 --port 8080
```

The GGUF metadata carries the ChatML-style chat template, so conversation formatting is automatic in recent llama.cpp versions.

### Which file is picked by default

Without `--hf-file`, llama.cpp searches the repo for `Q4_K_M`, then `Q8_0`, and otherwise falls back
to the first GGUF it finds. In this repo that resolves to
**`MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Instruct-Q8_0.gguf` (387 MB)** — note this is *not* the QAT `Q4_1` build.
To select a quant explicitly, either pass `--hf-file` as above, or use the shorthand tag form:

```
llama-cli -hf taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-GGUF:Q4_1
```

## Files

| File | Size | Converted from | Pick it when |
|------|------|----------------|--------------|
| `MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Instruct-F16.gguf` | 726 MB | BF16 instruction-tuned checkpoint | you want the reference quality / plan to fine-tune |
| `MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Instruct-Q8_0.gguf` | 387 MB | BF16 instruction-tuned checkpoint | desktop CPU with room to spare |
| `MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Instruct-Q4_1.gguf` | 192 MB | QAT checkpoint (see below) | memory-constrained / on-device, best size-quality ratio |

## QAT Q4_1 GGUF

The quantization-aware-training checkpoint is available as
[`MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Instruct-Q4_1.gguf`](https://huggingface.co/taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-GGUF/blob/main/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Instruct-Q4_1.gguf).

This is distinct from the BF16-derived `F16` / `Q8_0` files: Q4_1 is converted from the QAT
checkpoint, i.e. the model was trained with quantization in the loop rather than quantized
after the fact, so it keeps near-BF16 accuracy at a 4-bit footprint.

```shell
llama-cli -hf taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-GGUF \
  --hf-file MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Instruct-Q4_1.gguf \
  -p "What is MNN?"
```

## Model Details

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Parameters | ~300M |
| Architecture | Decoder-only transformer, 28 layers |
| Hidden size | 896 |
| Attention | 14 heads, GQA with 2 KV heads, head_dim 64 |
| FFN intermediate | 2560 (SiLU) |
| Context Length | 32K (40,960 position embeddings) |
| Vocabulary | 65,536 |
| Embeddings | tied input/output |
| Chat template | ChatML-style (embedded in GGUF metadata) |
| Languages | Chinese, English |

### Chat Template

ChatML-style conversation format; the template is embedded in the GGUF metadata, so llama.cpp
enters conversation mode automatically — no extra flag needed. Schematic:

```
[IM_START]system
You are a helpful assistant.[IM_END]
[IM_START]user
Hello![IM_END]
[IM_START]assistant
```

## 📊 Benchmarks

Scores of the underlying model (higher is better). `F16` / `Q8_0` track the BF16 column, `Q4_1`
tracks the INT4 (QAT) column.

| Benchmark   | BF16  | INT4 (QAT) | Gemma-3-270M | ERNIE-4.5-0.3B | LFM2.5-350M | SmolLM2-360M | Hunyuan-0.5B | MiniCPM4-0.5B | Qwen3-0.6B |
|-------------|-------|------------|--------------|----------------|-------------|--------------|--------------|---------------|------------|
| **Average** | 50.00 | 49.59      | 6.42         | 31.99          | 31.28       | 18.43        | 31.22        | 46.81         | 44.28      |
| C-Eval      | 38.86 | 40.27      | 6.84         | 32.17          | 32.10       | 23.77        | 35.29        | 67.98         | 44.06      |
| CMMLU       | 40.11 | 39.65      | 4.94         | 33.91          | 31.65       | 24.87        | 35.69        | 66.04         | 44.50      |
| MMLU-Redux  | 44.00 | 43.40      | 13.58        | 32.68          | 41.01       | 24.17        | 36.29        | 52.85         | 51.63      |
| BBH         | 47.38 | 46.63      | 8.09         | 31.07          | 26.03       | 27.74        | 54.65        | 47.61         | 41.94      |
| IFEval      | 73.20 | 74.12      | 20.15        | 44.92          | 72.09       | 32.16        | 24.58        | 52.13         | 56.93      |
| IFEval-zh   | 74.59 | 72.49      | 17.02        | 32.87          | 44.06       | 25.64        | 25.87        | 30.30         | 50.35      |
| GSM8K       | 54.36 | 52.84      | 0.00         | 31.24          | 33.66       | 11.60        | 36.01        | 42.46         | 45.49      |
| MGSM-zh     | 51.20 | 48.80      | 0.00         | 25.20          | 18.00       | 3.60         | 34.80        | 37.60         | 40.00      |
| MATH500     | 35.40 | 35.40      | 0.00         | 21.40          | 14.80       | 4.60         | 35.80        | 23.00         | 45.20      |
| HumanEval   | 53.66 | 53.66      | 0.00         | 38.41          | 14.63       | 0.00         | 14.63        | 48.17         | 36.59      |
| MBPP        | 37.20 | 38.20      | 0.00         | 28.00          | 16.00       | 24.60        | 9.80         | 46.80         | 30.40      |

## Other Formats

- [MNN-Pocket-0.3B](https://huggingface.co/taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B) — BF16 safetensors, full model card (723 MB)
- [MNN-Pocket-0.3B-MNN](https://huggingface.co/taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-MNN) — INT4 W4A16 QAT build for the MNN runtime (173 MB)
- [MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Base](https://huggingface.co/taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Base) / [MNN-Pocket-0.3B-SFT](https://huggingface.co/taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-SFT) — pre-training / SFT checkpoints
- [MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Dec](https://huggingface.co/taobao-mnn/MNN-Pocket-0.3B-Dec) — non-autoregressive decision model (LoRA adapter + pointer head)

